<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Itakhuli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1682">1682</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-mughal-conflicts">Ahom–Mughal conflicts</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Itakhuli was fought in 1682 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guwahati">Guwahati</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the Ahom kingdom and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. Ahom forces sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gadadhar-singha">Gadadhar Singha</a> defeated the Mughal garrison and drove it west beyond the Manas river. It was the last battle of the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-mughal-conflicts">Ahom–Mughal conflicts</a>, and it left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahoms</a> in control of western Assam until the British conquest.</p></div>
